  "id": "COMPOUND:18584 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Zizyberenalic acid appears to interact with the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular pathways, primarily via the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Zizyberenalic acid, and is itself a target of other molecules such as 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. The presence of multiple targets suggests a potential role in the regulation of choline transport, possibly through the modulation of sialyltransferase activity, which is involved in the synthesis of sialic acid. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Zizyberenalic acid influences choline transport, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence suggests a complex network of molecular relationships, where Zizyberenalic acid may act as a modulator of choline transporter activity through indirect pathways involving sialyltransferases.",
